{
  "id": "tokio_rs_tokio_8440",
  "repo_name": "tokio-rs/tokio",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio",
  "base_commit": "022c004b4a7c42c0c534e9737e9c66ff916517b1",
  "pr_number": 8440,
  "issue_number": 8433,
  "issue_title": "ci: io_uring latest-kernel leg reports \"all tests passed\" after `fs_uring` is OOM-killed inside QEMU; the remaining test binaries never run, and `fs_uring_statx::stat_permission_denied` fails once they do",
  "issue_body": "The `Test io_uring on Linux <latest-stable>` job ([`uring-kernel-version-test.yml`](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/blob/d6bf379eba23fbe2dc334b2da4e3d28ee65e5ffd/.github/workflows/uring-kernel-version-test.yml), called from `ci.yml` on every push and PR) is green on every retained master run, but inside the guest `fs_uring` is OOM-killed during `open_many_files`, init dies with it, and the 10 binaries that sort after it (the other `fs_uring_*` suites, `fs_write`, and the `tokio` lib test binary) never execute. The step still prints `all tests passed` because a SIGKILLed binary never writes the `test result: FAILED` line the step greps for, and QEMU exits 0 after the resulting kernel panic under `panic=1 -no-reboot`. Giving the guest enough memory shows what the green was hiding: `fs_uring_statx::stat_permission_denied` fails on 7.2.4, because the guest runs the tests as root and a `0o244` directory does not stop root. The job exists to \"run fs tests on the latest linux kernel, ensuring tokio's io_uring apis don't break on the latest kernel\" (#7486).\n\n**Reproduction**, from the latest master run [34219362392](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/actions/runs/34219362392) (d6bf379e):\n\n```\ngh run view 34219362392 -R tokio-rs/tokio --job 102039005349 --log \\\n  | grep -E 'running [0-9]+ tests?|Out of memory|Attempted to kill init|all tests passed'\n```\n\nOn the 7.2.4 job ([102039005349](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/actions/runs/34219362392/job/102039005349)) this prints 15 `running N tests` lines, then:\n\n```\ntest open_many_files ... [   72.915500] tokio-rt-worker invoked oom-killer: ...\n[   72.927912] Out of memory: Killed process 175 (fs_uring-da0323) total-vm:285332kB, anon-rss:205708kB, file-rss:31116kB, ...\n[   72.970629] Kernel panic - not syncing: Attempted to kill init! exitcode=0x00008900\nall tests passed\n```\n\nThe 4.19.325 control job in the same run ([102039005534](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/actions/runs/34219362392/job/102039005534)) prints 25 `running N tests` lines, including `running 200 tests` for the lib binary, before `Attempted to kill init! exitcode=0x00000000` and `all tests passed`.\n\n**Mechanism.** init runs `for f in /bin/tests/*; do RUST_BACKTRACE=1 \"$f\" ; done` under `set -e` ([L74\u2013L83](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/blob/d6bf379eba23fbe2dc334b2da4e3d28ee65e5ffd/.github/workflows/uring-kernel-version-test.yml#L74-L83)). `fs_uring` sorts first among the io_uring binaries (`-` before `_`), and `open_many_files` (512 files, 10 000 spawned opens, [`fs_uring.rs#L88-L98`](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/blob/d6bf379eba23fbe2dc334b2da4e3d28ee65e5ffd/tokio/tests/fs_uring.rs#L88-L98)) reaches 200\u2013340 MB anon RSS in a `-m 1024` guest where ~746 MiB is already unevictable, because the initramfs holds the unstripped musl debug binaries (cpio archive 1 528 706 blocks, \u2248783 MB). The kernel kills the test, init exits 137, the kernel panics (`exitcode=0x00008900`), and with `panic=1` + `-no-reboot` QEMU shuts down with status 0, so the `qemu_status` check from #8271 passes (`-action panic=exit-failure` changes nothing: the 4.19 leg also ends in `Attempted to kill init` and QEMU exits 0 there too). The last gate, `grep -q \"test result: FAILED\"` ([L115](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/blob/d6bf379eba23fbe2dc334b2da4e3d28ee65e5ffd/.github/workflows/uring-kernel-version-test.yml#L115)), cannot see a binary killed before it printed a summary. #8271's description names exactly this gap: \"The log check only recognizes Rust's `test result: FAILED` text, so it is not a substitute for QEMU's exit status\" \u2014 and #8271's own merge run has the same OOM kill under a green step.\n\nThe pattern is identical in the oldest retained latest-kernel log and at a midpoint, so it is at least 77 days old; the onset is beyond log retention:\n\n- 2026-06-23, kernel 7.1.1, job [82908203355](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/actions/runs/28010858949/job/82908203355): `Killed process 172 (fs_uring-dface4) ... anon-rss:337824kB`, `exitcode=0x00008900`, `all tests passed`\n- 2026-07-14, kernel 7.1.3, the #8271 merge commit, job [87030454316](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/actions/runs/29316037791/job/87030454316): `Killed process 170 (fs_uring-f74528) ... anon-rss:314564kB`, same\n- 2026-09-08, kernel 7.2.4, job [102039005349](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/actions/runs/34219362392/job/102039005349): above\n\nThe OOM cannot predate `open_many_files` (#7321, 2025-08-08 \u2014 ADD-SP's review there: \"nit: 10,000 is a little bit large, so `TaskTracker` might saves memory when running this test\"); the detection gap dates from the workflow's introduction in #7486, whose original comment read `# qemu always exits with 0, so we check if the tests passed by using grep.` `stat_permission_denied` was added in #8080 (2026-06-13) and has not executed on the latest-kernel leg in any retained run, including #8080's own.\n\n**Fork runs**, the unchanged tree at d6bf379e plus a one-file harness that calls the reusable workflow with `kernel_version: 7.2.4`:\n\n- baseline, twice: [34248671250](https://github.com/glaziermag/tokio/actions/runs/34248671250), [34253085790](https://github.com/glaziermag/tokio/actions/runs/34253085790) \u2014 green, same OOM kill and `exitcode=0x00008900` in the log\n- init echoes `ALL_TESTS_COMPLETED` after the loop and the step requires it: [34248665407](https://github.com/glaziermag/tokio/actions/runs/34248665407) \u2014 red, `tests did not run to completion`\n- the same plus `-m 3072`: [34248668864](https://github.com/glaziermag/tokio/actions/runs/34248668864), [34253169801](https://github.com/glaziermag/tokio/actions/runs/34253169801) \u2014 `open_many_files` completes, 22 of 25 binaries run, then `fs_uring_statx` reports `stat_permission_denied ... FAILED` (`called Option::unwrap() on a None value` at [`fs_uring_statx.rs:181`](https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/blob/d6bf379eba23fbe2dc334b2da4e3d28ee65e5ffd/tokio/tests/fs_uring_statx.rs#L156-L184): the guest is `UID: 0`, so `try_exists` on the file under the `0o244` directory returns `Ok` instead of `EACCES`), init exits 101, the step fails with `tests reported failures`. On 4.19 the test returns early at `io_uring_supported()`, and the `ubuntu-latest, io-uring` nextest job runs it unprivileged, which is why it passes everywhere else.\n\nTwo ways to resolve it:\n\n1. Require a completion marker from init (diff below), give the guest enough memory for the suite (`-m 3072`, or strip the test binaries so the initramfs stops taking most of the 1 GiB), and make `stat_permission_denied` root-aware (return early when `libc::geteuid() == 0`, or run the guest binaries as an unprivileged user). The leg then goes red on any future early exit \u2014 panic, OOM, killed binary \u2014 and covers all 25 binaries on the latest kernel. This is what I'd do.\n2. Add only the completion marker and let the leg go red, treating the OOM (`open_many_files` holding 200\u2013340 MB for 10 000 in-flight opens) and the root assumption as two follow-ups to look at on their own.\n\n```diff\n           for f in /bin/tests/*; do RUST_BACKTRACE=1 \"$f\" ; done\n+          echo \"ALL_TESTS_COMPLETED\"\n           EOF\n@@\n           if grep -q \"test result: FAILED\" qemu-output.log; then\n             echo \"tests reported failures\"\n             exit 1\n-          else\n-            echo \"all tests passed\"\n           fi\n+\n+          if ! grep -q \"ALL_TESTS_COMPLETED\" qemu-output.log; then\n+            echo \"tests did not run to completion (init exited before the last test binary)\"\n+            exit 1\n+          fi\n+\n+          echo \"all tests passed\"\n```\n\nI found this while auditing the io_uring CI legs after #8389, verified the job logs and step conclusions via the Actions API, and reproduced it on the fork runs linked above. I used AI assistance (Claude) for the investigation and drafting; I've reviewed it and stand behind it.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-09-10T13:09:50Z",
